        "statement": "For $n\\not\\equiv1\\pmod3$, $\\nu_2(W_n)=n$.\nThe positive normalized determinants at $n=3m$ and $n=3m+2$ represent the\nsame square class in $\\mathbb Q_{>0}^{\\times}/(\\mathbb Q_{>0}^{\\times})^2$,\nnamely the class of $d_m$.\nMoreover, replacing $3^{n-3r}$ in the definition of $w_n$ by\n$a^{n-3r}$ for any $a\\in\\RR$ leaves every $W_n$ unchanged.",
