        "statement": "For real $a,t$ define\n\\[\n w_j(a,t)=\\sum_{r=0}^{\\lfloor j/3\\rfloor}\n  \\binom j{3r}a^{j-3r}t^r c_r,\\qquad\n H_n(a,t)=(w_{i+j}(a,t))_{0\\leq i,j\\leq n}.\n\\]\nFor $t\\ne0$, the inertia of $H_n(a,t)$, listed as the numbers of positive,\nnegative and zero eigenvalues, is\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|c}\nn&\\operatorname{inertia} H_n(a,t)\\\\\\hline\n3m&(2m+1,m,0)\\\\\n3m+1&(2m+1,m,1)\\\\\n3m+2&(2m+2,m+1,0).\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nIn particular, every zero in the original determinant family has nullity\nexactly one. For $n\\not\\equiv1\\pmod3$,\n\\[\n \\det H_n(a,t)=t^{n(n+1)/3}W_n.\n\\]\nFor $t=0$, the inertia is $(1,0,n)$ and the determinant is $1$ at $n=0$\nand $0$ otherwise. For nonzero integers $t$ and $n\\not\\equiv1\\pmod3$,\n\\[\n \\nu_2(\\det H_n(a,t))=n+\\frac{n(n+1)}3\\nu_2(t)\n \\quad\\text{when }a\\in\\ZZ.\n\\]",
