        "statement": "For every real $\\alpha>0$ and integer $n\\geq1$, with\n$h_j=\\sum_{k=1}^j k^{-\\alpha}$ and $h_0=0$,\n\\[\n (-1)^n\\det(h_{i+j})_{0\\leq i,j\\leq n}>0.\n\\]\nThus Sun's v5 Conjecture 3.9(i), p.~15, holds for every positive integer\norder, and also for every positive real order. For order one, a prior\nexact evaluation follows from Petrov's answer of February 16, 2017,\nCigler's completion of February 17, and Amdeberhan's independent identity\nproof of February 18; see also Cigler, Theorem 4.1, equation (4.2)\\cite{harmonic}.",
